7 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566877 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186566501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566877 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "02a5f76b-f604-59fe-97b6-05e2a5373e9f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566894 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566894 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566393 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566894 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566894 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566894 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566894 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566894 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566894 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186566478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566894 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566956 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566956 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566956 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566743 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566956 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566956 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566956 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566956 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566956 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186566670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566956 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567008 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567008 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181972" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567008 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567008 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=Z\\times {Z}_{0}^{-}$ in the Cartesian plane?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567008 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "025f0441-54cd-515d-9989-fed405f3f4cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567008 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=Z\\times {Z}_{0}^{-}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is an integer number and whose $y$-coordinate is a negative integer or zero..\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in Z,\\,y\\in {Z}_{0}^{-}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is negative integer or zero.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}=\\{(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in {Z}_{0}^{-}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/a5/a5d50bdd40efb18b4d29f3e108576e3befcc0d3f3e5b54a0686aeef6e9ffa212.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any negative integer or zero.\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in {Z}_{0}^{-}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/12/129cb0ae2a59415a90118030461244ab7f1faa91aba47b5e0e2864323dbfede9.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-3},{S}_{-2},{S}_{0},{S}_{2},{S}_{3},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =…\\cup {S}_{-3}\\cup {S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in Z}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $Z\\times {Z}_{0}^{-}$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/25/25bd7ebe8087af06fa21e4d5f9878d0e5867630372138bad1af241c1ee270d30.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567019 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567019 #edb/ref 1069 "q-184529" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567019 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567019 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[i,1]\\times \\{i\\}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567019 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "151c9aa4-1f7d-5ae4-bc54-fb829989618a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567019 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0.5,1]\\times \\{0.5\\}=\\{(k,0.5)\\,:\\,k\\in [0.5,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(0.5,0.5)$ to the point $(1,0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/bb/bb8f515fb5c342ece5727830e95bcc617c03a5bf6542f959ba9e020d22f7faef.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[i,1]\\times \\{i\\}=\\{(k,i)\\,:\\,k\\in [i,1]\\}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(i,i)$ to the point $(1,i).$ \n\n![](images/f2/f255d7dede080e93cb135c1087a0f14591467439d891187062a4fa185a8858cf.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/d8/d823dd4dcd675b07b004cf2850059600e861c8b3d259f884d25c61e43431de35.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567095 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567095 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181780" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567095 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567095 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S={R}^{+}\\times Z$ in the Cartesian plane?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567095 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e159fb00-748b-54e2-99d5-3850d85771a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567095 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS={R}^{+}\\times Z\n$$\n\n \ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a positive real number and whose $y$-coordinate is an integer number.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in {R}^{+},\\,y\\in Z\\}\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S,$ consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any positive real number and whose $y$-coordinate equals $-1.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}=\\{(x,-1)\\,:\\,x\\in {R}^{+}\\}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/50/50228bcff5b3678518379cda03257ac234e8312cd23f9b38fa897188c8c5c1c5.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any positive real number and whose $y$-coordinate equals $1.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(x,1)\\,:\\,x\\in {R}^{+}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/75/75f8be8dd49241503b705c78e4018a98fead197191b38f856d7fbce069a63de2.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-3},{S}_{-2},{S}_{0},{S}_{2},{S}_{3},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product consists of the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{+}\\times Z & =…{S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in Z}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize ${R}^{+}\\times Z$ as the set of horizontal lines shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/20/2086bcf65608ff2c031da9f6882272fd6d8eb828f3d904c4f0fc946b5fbe108c.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567118 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "25a9e4f2-d080-581c-9f8c-5e235244e694" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567118 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186567019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567123 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186567136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567123 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "40115689-6ef7-5297-b4cc-659f1af4234d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567123 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186567095 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567135 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186567123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567135 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8b7cd465-a531-5b2c-aa31-225a1dbba8b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567135 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567136 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186567138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567136 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "929b7ead-827c-5b82-82c3-38ca98ce721d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567136 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186287775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567138 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186567118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567138 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9b20313e-470b-5bfd-bcdb-18795605d3de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186567138 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186567008 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
